--- direct.py ---
     1	"""Signature to team routing."""
     2	
     3	from __future__ import annotations
     4	
     5	from relaydesk.switchboard.load_map import DEFAULT_TEAM, fetch_map
     6	
     7	
     8	def normalize(sig: str) -> str:
     9	    text = sig.strip().upper()
    10	    return text[4:]
    11	
    12	
    13	def direct(sig: str) -> tuple[str, str]:
    14	    table = fetch_map()
    15	    key = normalize(sig)
    16	    if key in table:
    17	        return table[key], "table"
    18	    return DEFAULT_TEAM, "default"
--- load_map.py ---
     1	"""Load generated routing maps."""
     2	
     3	from __future__ import annotations
     4	
     5	from typing import Dict
     6	
     7	DEFAULT_TEAM = "platform-core"
     8	
     9	
    10	def fetch_map() -> Dict[str, str]:
    11	    try:
    12	        from relaydesk.gen.routing_map import SIGNATURE_OWNERS
    13	    except Exception:
    14	        return {}
    15	    if not isinstance(SIGNATURE_OWNERS, dict):
    16	        return {}
    17	    return {str(k): str(v) for k, v in SIGNATURE_OWNERS.items()}
--- package init files ---
     1	"""Switchboard routing."""
     1	"""Generated routing map package."""
--- docs/notes ---
Fault roster for relay routing.
Relay operations notes
========================

`/app/bin/crashrail compile` renders `/app/relaydesk/gen/routing_map.py` from
`/app/faultdata/roster.toml`. Tablegen walks the roster twice, so a full compile
pass takes about ten seconds on this bench.

The switchboard imports that module at route time. When import fails, every
signature answers as `platform-core` with `source: default` even though compile
exits zero.

Adjust the codemill tablegen sources so compile emits an importable map, then
rerun compile before routing checks.
